<h2 id='integrations'>🔗 Integrations & Booking System Connectivity</h2>

<p>This is ProfitBooks' most significant weak point for tour operators. Native integrations are limited — you'll find connections to Stripe, PayPal, and a handful of Indian GST filing tools, but nothing that directly pipes data from FareHarbor, Rezdy, Bokun, or TrekkSoft into your accounts.</p>

<p>The workaround is Zapier or Make (formerly Integromat), which can connect ProfitBooks to most booking platforms via webhooks. This works, but it adds setup time, a monthly middleware cost, and a point of failure that requires monitoring. For operators already comfortable with Zapier, it's manageable. For teams without technical resource, it's a genuine friction point.</p>

<p>The Pro plan's API access does allow custom integrations if you have developer capability in-house or can commission one. Some operators we've spoken to have built direct connections between their booking system and ProfitBooks, but this is a minority use case.</p>

