<h2 id='who-its-for'>🎯 Who ProfitBooks Is For</h2>

<p><strong>Best fit:</strong> Independent tour operators and small-to-mid travel companies running up to 50 departures per month who need reliable multi-currency invoicing, expense tracking, and clean financial reports without enterprise pricing or a steep learning curve. Particularly strong for operators selling into multiple international markets who are currently handling FX manually.</p>

<p><strong>Also works well for:</strong> Operators who handle their own bookkeeping without a dedicated accountant, businesses transitioning off spreadsheets for the first time, and companies that want a low-cost solution while they scale toward a tool like Xero.</p>

<p><strong>Not the right fit if:</strong> You need per-departure profitability reporting built natively, seamless two-way sync with your booking platform, global payroll processing, or the deep reporting customization that Xero or QuickBooks Enterprise provide. If your operation is running 200+ departures monthly across multiple entities, you'll outgrow ProfitBooks relatively quickly.</p>

